From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:48:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] WebSocket: connect through the configured HTTP or SOCKS5
 proxy

WsFramedStream ignored the proxy setting (`to-do: websocket proxy`), so a
client in WebSocket mode could not reach its server from networks where
traffic may only leave through a proxy, the networks WebSocket mode is
for. With a proxy configured, open an HTTP CONNECT or SOCKS5 tunnel to the
server first, using the existing Proxy code, and run TLS and the WebSocket
handshake over it. HTTPS proxies are not supported yet and fail with an
explicit error; without a proxy the connection is made as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
